{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a606b9ba1ebbb0da9","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EdjoTJD9HndCYCaGB7WVEa","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-UPA1nu/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-oyxCox/9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d/tasks/a606b9ba1ebbb0da9.output","summary":"Done. `translation/src/compress/huf_compress.rs` is complete: **2000 lines**, translating all 33 functions of `c_src/src/compress/huf_compress.c` in source order.\n\n## Exported symbols (15, all `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn`)\nVerified against `c_syms.txt` (`nm` list) — exactly the non-`static` set, no more, no less:\n\n`HUF_readCTableHeader`, `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`, `HUF_readCTable`, `HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable`, `HUF_buildCTable_wksp`, `HUF_estimateCompressedSize`, `HUF_validateCTable`, `HUF_compressBound`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable`, `HUF_compress4X_usingCTable`, `HUF_cardinality`, `HUF_minTableLog`, `HUF_optimalTableLog`, `HUF_compress1X_repeat`, `HUF_compress4X_repeat`\n\nI confirmed these 15 actually appear in `nm -D` of a built `.so`. Note the task list omitted `HUF_compressBound`'s companion — it was there — and the list matched otherwise.\n\n## Internal (private `unsafe fn`, no mangling)\n`HUF_alignUpWorkspace`, `HUF_compressWeights`, `HUF_getNbBits/Fast`, `HUF_getValue/Fast`, `HUF_setNbBits`, `HUF_setValue`, `HUF_writeCTableHeader`, `HUF_setMaxHeight`, `HUF_getIndex`, `HUF_swapNodes`, `HUF_isSorted`, `HUF_insertionSort`, `HUF_quickSortPartition`, `HUF_simpleQuickSort`, `HUF_sort`, `HUF_buildTree`, `HUF_buildCTableFromTree`, `HUF_initCStream`, `HUF_addBits`, `HUF_zeroIndex1`, `HUF_mergeIndex1`, `HUF_flushBits`, `HUF_endMark`, `HUF_closeCStream`, `HUF_encodeSymbol`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal_body_loop`, `HUF_tightCompressBound`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal_body`, `HUF_compress1X/4X_usingCTable_internal`, `HUF_compressCTable_internal`, `HUF_compress_internal`. Types: `nodeElt`, `rankPos`, `huffNodeTable`, `HUF_CStream_t`, `HUF_CompressWeightsWksp`, `HUF_WriteCTableWksp`, `HUF_buildCTable_wksp_tables`, `HUF_compress_tables_t` (+ its `#[repr(C)] union` of wksps), `HUF_nbStreams_e`.\n\n## Build status\n`cd translation && cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep huf_compress` → **no output**: zero errors and zero warnings attributed to my file. The 67 remaining crate errors are all in other modules that are still empty stubs (`compress/zstd_compress.rs`, `zstd_double_fast.rs`, `deprecated/zbuff_compress.rs`, `legacy/*`, etc.) — none reference `huf_compress`.\n\n`hist.rs`, `fse_compress.rs`, and `entropy_common.rs` were empty when I started but have since been filled in by other work, so my `crate::compress::hist::{HIST_count_simple, HIST_count_wksp, HIST_WKSP_SIZE_U32}`, `crate::compress::fse_compress::{FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, FSE_normalizeCount, FSE_writeNCount, FSE_buildCTable_wksp, FSE_compress_usingCTable}`, and `crate::entropy_common::HUF_readStats` imports all resolve and type-check against the real signatures.\n\nI also built an isolated scratch crate (in `$TMPDIR`, not the repo) with only huf_compress + its deps, to confirm the module fully type-checks and links rather than being skipped due to name-resolution failures elsewhere. Layout was asserted there via temporary `const _: () = assert!(...)`:\n- `size_of::<nodeElt>() == 8`\n- `size_of::<HUF_buildCTable_wksp_tables>() == HUF_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE` (4864) — the C `HUF_STATIC_ASSERT`\n- `HUF_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE >= size_of::<HUF_WriteCTableWksp>()`\n- `size_of::<HUF_compress_tables_t>() + HUF_WORKSPACE_MAX_ALIGNMENT <= HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE`\n- `size_of::<HUF_CElt>() == size_of::<HUF_CTableHeader>()`\n\n## Translation notes worth flagging\n- `DYNAMIC_BMI2=0`: `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable_internal` collapses to a direct call of `_body`; the `_bmi2`/`_default` pair and all asm variants are gone. `flags` is kept in the signature but unused, as in C.\n- All `assert()`/`DEBUGLOG()`/`RAWLOG()` dropped, including the `DEBUGLEVEL>=2` `showU32`/`showCTableBits`/`showHNodeSymbols`/`showHNodeBits` helpers (compiled out) and the `DEBUGLEVEL>=1` block inside `HUF_addBits`.\n- `RANK_POSITION_DISTINCT_COUNT_CUTOFF` is a macro whose expansion calls `ZSTD_highbit32`, which isn't `const fn` in `crate::bits`, so it became a `#[inline(always)] fn` evaluated at each use site — matching the C macro's per-use expansion. (Its value is 165; the C comment claims 166, which is wrong but harmless — I preserved the computation, not the comment.)\n- Two intentional C quirks preserved rather than \"fixed\": `wksp->huffWeight[maxSymbolValue] = 0` in `HUF_writeCTable_wksp` writes one byte past the 255-element array when `maxSymbolValue == 255` (done via raw-pointer `.add()`); and `HUF_flushBits`'s `bitContainer >> (64 - nbBits)` uses `wrapping_shr` so an `nbBits == 0` case reproduces the x86 shift-masking the C relies on instead of being UB.\n- Wrapping arithmetic made explicit where C's unsigned/int conversions can overflow: `totalCost` accumulation in `HUF_setMaxHeight` (`int += unsigned` round-trip), `bitPos` accumulation in `HUF_addBits`/`HUF_mergeIndex1` (dirty high bits are expected), `srcSize - 1` in `HUF_compressCTable_internal`, and `128 + (maxSymbolValue - 1)` in `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`.\n- `for`-loop `continue` semantics were preserved carefully in the three places where C's increment expression still runs on `continue` (`HUF_setMaxHeight`'s two loops, `HUF_optimalTableLog`'s search loop) — a spot where a naive `while` translation would silently infinite-loop.","usage":{"total_tokens":159569,"tool_uses":34,"duration_ms":667369},"uuid":"07bec7c4-3f85-48bf-bac0-1fa33d4f9836","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d"}
