{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QDM6DjoPMzkhfhhWhBpNn6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# zstd C -> Rust transliteration guide (MANDATORY reading)\n2\t\n3\tGoal: a **mechanical, semantics-preserving transliteration** of the C in `c_src/`\n4\tinto Rust in `translation/src/`. The Rust cdylib must export the same public\n5\tsymbols and produce byte-identical results. Do NOT redesign, do NOT \"improve\",\n6\tdo NOT fix bugs. Keep function order, check order, and arithmetic exactly.\n7\t\n8\t## Build configuration (already fixed, do not change)\n9\t* `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`, `XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_`, `DYNAMIC_BMI2=0`\n10\t* `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` is **NOT** defined  -> threading/pool are no-ops\n11\t* `DEBUGLEVEL` is 0 -> `assert()`, `DEBUGLOG()`, `RAWLOG()` are **no-ops**:\n12\t  simply drop them. Never translate an `assert()` into a Rust `assert!`.\n13\t* `ZSTD_TRACE == 1` (weak symbols available) but the hooks are never defined,\n14\t  so they are always NULL. `crate::zstd_trace` provides\n15\t  `ZSTD_trace_compress_begin` etc. as `None`. Keep the NULL checks.\n16\t* No ASAN / MSAN -> drop all `__asan_*` / `__msan_*` code.\n17\t* Target is x86-64 little-endian, 64-bit.\n18\t\n19\t## Crate layout\n20\t```\n21\ttranslation/src/\n22\t  lib.rs                     module list\n23\t  cmem.rs                    mem.h  (MEM_read*/MEM_write*/MEM_swap*, ZSTD_memcpy/memmove/memset/memcmp,\n24\t                             malloc/calloc/free externs, type aliases BYTE,U8,S8,U16,S16,U32,S32,U64,S64)\n25\t  bits.rs                    bits.h (ZSTD_highbit32, ZSTD_countTrailingZeros*, ZSTD_NbCommonBytes, ZSTD_rotateRight_*)\n26\t  error_private.rs           zstd_errors.h + error_private.{h,c}\n27\t                             `ERROR(ZSTD_error_xxx)` -> usize;  ERR_isError, ERR_getErrorCode, ERR_getErrorName\n28\t  bitstream.rs               bitstream.h (BIT_CStream_t, BIT_DStream_t, BIT_* fns)\n29\t  fse.rs                     fse.h  (constants, FSE_CState_t, FSE_DState_t, inline fns)\n30\t  huf.rs                     huf.h  (constants, HUF_CElt, HUF_DTable, HUF_CTableHeader)\n31\t  xxhash.rs                  xxhash (XXH32/XXH64; exported as ZSTD_XXH32... )\n32\t  zstd_h.rs                  public zstd.h constants/enums/structs\n33\t  zstd_internal.rs           zstd_internal.h + allocations.h  (tables, ZSTD_wildcopy, ZSTD_customMalloc, ...)\n34\t  zstd_trace.rs              zstd_trace.h\n35\t  zstd_common.rs             zstd_common.c\n36\t  pool.rs                    pool.c (non-MT) + threading.c + debug.c globals\n37\t  entropy_common.rs          common/entropy_common.c\n38\t  fse_decompress.rs          common/fse_decompress.c\n39\t  compress/mod.rs  + one file per c_src/src/compress/*.c and the shared headers\n40\t  decompress/mod.rs + one file per c_src/src/decompress/*.c\n41\t  dictbuilder/mod.rs + one file per c_src/src/dictBuilder/*.c\n42\t  deprecated/mod.rs + one file per c_src/src/deprecated/*.c\n43\t  legacy/mod.rs    + v01.rs .. v07.rs\n44\t```\n45\tShared *type* definitions already exist; **reuse them, never redefine**:\n46\t* `compress/zstd_cwksp.rs`            <- `zstd_cwksp.h`\n47\t* `compress/zstd_compress_internal.rs` <- `zstd_compress_internal.h`\n48\t  (SeqDef, SeqStore_t, ZSTD_MatchState_t, ZSTD_CCtx, ZSTD_CCtx_params, ZSTD_CDict,\n49\t   optState_t, ldmState_t, ldmParams_t, RawSeqStore_t, rawSeq, ZSTD_match_t,\n50\t   ZSTD_optimal_t, hashes, ZSTD_count, ZSTD_storeSeq, ZSTD_window_*, ...)\n51\t* `decompress/zstd_decompress_internal.rs` <- `zstd_decompress_internal.h`\n52\t  (ZSTD_DCtx, ZSTD_DDict, ZSTD_seqSymbol, ZSTD_entropyDTables_t, LL_base, OF_base, ML_base, ...)\n53\t\n54\tREAD those files before writing code so you use the exact names/types.\n55\t\n56\t## Style rules\n57\t\n58\t1. **Every file starts with**\n59\t   ```rust\n60\t   //! Translation of `<relative c path>`\n61\t   #![allow(dead_code)]\n62\t   ```\n63\t   and imports what it needs from `crate::...`.\n64\t\n65\t2. **Public C functions** (those visible in `nm -D` of the C .so) get\n66\t   ```rust\n67\t   #[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n68\t   pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn NAME(args...) -> Ret { ... }\n69\t   ```\n70\t   Use the exact final linker name (watch for `#define foo PREFIX_foo` macros,\n71\t   e.g. xxhash's `XXH_NAMESPACE`, and the legacy `FSEv05_`/`HUFv06_` renames).\n72\t   `static` C functions become plain `pub(crate) unsafe fn` (no `no_mangle`,\n73\t   no `extern \"C\"`) unless they are used as function pointers, in which case\n74\t   they must be `unsafe extern \"C\" fn` (but still no `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`).\n75\t\n76\t3. **Types**: map C to Rust as\n77\t   `size_t`->`usize`, `ptrdiff_t`->`isize`, `int`->`c_int`, `unsigned`->`c_uint`,\n78\t   `char`->`c_char`, `void*`->`*mut c_void`, `const void*`->`*const c_void`,\n79\t   `unsigned long long`->`u64`, `BYTE`->`u8`.\n80\t   Enums are `pub type X = c_uint;` + `pub const` values (already done for shared ones).\n81\t   Structs are `#[repr(C)]` with the **same field order** as C.\n82\t\n83\t4. **Arithmetic**: C has wrapping semantics for unsigned and (in practice) for\n84\t   signed. The crate is built with `overflow-checks = false`, but be explicit\n85\t   where overflow is expected: use `wrapping_add/sub/mul`, and for pointers use\n86\t   `(p as usize).wrapping_add(n) as *const T` style when the C code can create\n87\t   out-of-range pointers. Prefer `.add()/.sub()/.offset()` where valid.\n88\t   `a - b` on pointers -> `a.offset_from(b)` (isize) or\n89\t   `(a as usize) - (b as usize)`.\n90\t\n91\t5. **Shifts**: C `x << n` where n may equal the width is UB; reproduce the x86\n92\t   behaviour only if the C actually relies on it (rare). Otherwise plain `<<`.\n93\t\n94\t6. **`memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset`** -> `ZSTD_memcpy/ZSTD_memmove/ZSTD_memset`\n95\t   from `crate::cmem` (they take `*mut c_void`).\n96\t\n97\t7. **Control flow**: `do { X } while (cond);` becomes\n98\t   `loop { X; if !(cond) { break; } }`. `goto` becomes a labelled loop / early\n99\t   return; preserve semantics exactly. C `switch` fallthrough must be replicated\n100\t   by duplicating the code or restructuring carefully.\n101\t\n102\t8. **Macros** `RETURN_ERROR_IF(cond, err, ...)`,\n103\t   `RETURN_ERROR(err, ...)`, `FORWARD_IF_ERROR(e, ...)`, `CHECK_F(f)`:\n104\t   ```rust\n105\t   if cond { return ERROR(ZSTD_error_err); }\n106\t   return ERROR(ZSTD_error_err);\n107\t   { let e = expr; if ERR_isError(e) != 0 { return e; } }\n108\t   ```\n109\t   `MIN`/`MAX` -> explicit `if`/`.min()`/`.max()` (careful with mixed signs).\n110\t\n111\t9. **Static const tables** -> `static NAME: [T; N] = [...];`\n112\t   Function-local `static const` tables -> module-level `static`.\n113\t\n114\t10. **Function pointers** -> `Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...) -> R>`; a NULL\n115\t    check becomes `.is_none()`.\n116\t\n117\t11. Do NOT add bounds checks, `Option`, `Result`, slices, or iterators where the\n118\t    C used raw pointers. Raw pointers everywhere is expected and correct here.\n119\t\n120\t12. Never use `std::` collections or allocation; use the libc `malloc`/`free`\n121\t    externs from `crate::cmem` (via `ZSTD_customMalloc`/`ZSTD_customFree`).\n122\t\n123\t13. If a C construct genuinely cannot be expressed, leave a\n124\t    `/* TODO(port): ... */` comment — but this should essentially never happen.\n125\t\n126\t## Verification\n127\t`cd translation && cargo build --release` must succeed with no errors.\n128\tThen `nm -D --defined-only target/release/libzstd.so` must contain every symbol\n129\tthat the C build exports.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LiNjQUo2FonajCKATeVvei","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d","uuid":"ed9a936d-78ca-4e49-bd54-ad528d64a033","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:21:14.598Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Port dictBuilder zdict.c"}
