S_HEAPMODE, ZSTD_HASHLOG3_MAX, ZSTD_NO_CLEVEL, ZSTD_INDEXOVERFLOW_MARGIN, srcSizeTiers, ZSTD_compResetPolicy_e {ZSTDcrp_makeClean, ZSTDcrp_leaveDirty}, ZSTD_indexResetPolicy_e {ZSTDirp_continue, ZSTDirp_reset}, ZSTD_resetTarget_e {ZSTD_resetTarget_CDict, ZSTD_resetTarget_CCtx}`\n\n## Two deviations worth flagging\n1. **`ZSTD_defaultCMem` is a `pub const`, not a `pub static`.** `ZSTD_customMem` contains a raw pointer so it is not `Sync`, and a `static` of it fails to compile. It is not an exported symbol in the C build (absent from `c_syms.txt`) and every use site copies it by value, so `const` is behaviourally identical. `crate::compress::zstd_compress::ZSTD_defaultCMem` resolves for other parts either way.\n2. **`ZSTD_initStaticCCtx` uses `ZSTD_cpuSupportsBmi2()`** where C writes `ZSTD_cpuid_bmi2(ZSTD_cpuid())`. The port's `crate::zstd_internal::ZSTD_cpuSupportsBmi2()` returns 0 unconditionally (per the pre-existing cpu.h translation), and with `DYNAMIC_BMI2 == 0` `cctx->bmi2` never selects a code path, so output is unaffected. A comment marks it.\n\nAlso note: `ZSTD_getSeqStore`'s C signature returns `const SeqStore_t*` — I kept `*const SeqStore_t`; and `ZSTD_CCtx_refThreadPool` takes `*mut crate::pool::POOL_ctx` (C `ZSTD_threadPool*` == `POOL_ctx*`).","usage":{"total_tokens":238036,"tool_uses":43,"duration_ms":681676},"uuid":"0aee7eca-045e-497d-80aa-d6d0fc0133dd","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d"}
