{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ab2ba2ca8e9b1df61","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ShdkyTvXzGQ2DbcP8gMmuT","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-UPA1nu/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-oyxCox/9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d/tasks/ab2ba2ca8e9b1df61.output","summary":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/translation/src/legacy/v02.rs` — **3536 lines**, **0 errors / 0 warnings** attributed to this file.\n\n### Exported symbols (verified via `nm -D` on an isolated build)\n`ZSTDv02_isError`, `ZSTDv02_decompress`, `ZSTDv02_findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`, `ZSTDv02_createDCtx`, `ZSTDv02_freeDCtx`, `ZSTDv02_resetDCtx`, `ZSTDv02_nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `ZSTDv02_decompressContinue` — exactly 8, all `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn`, signatures matching `zstd_v02.h`. Everything else is module-private (`unsafe fn`, or `unsafe extern \"C\" fn` without `no_mangle` for the three `HUF_decompress4X{2,4,6}` function-pointer targets).\n\n### Key finding — error code values\n`zstd_v02.c` includes `../common/error_private.h` **before** its own private error block, and both use the guard `ERROR_H_MODULE`. The legacy block is therefore **preprocessed away**: the legacy 10-value `ERR_codes` enum, `ERR_strings` and legacy `ERR_getErrorName` are never compiled. The real `ERROR(x)` / `ERR_isError` come from modern `error_private.h` with the modern `zstd_errors.h` values (`srcSize_wrong=72`, `corruption_detected=20`, `dstSize_tooSmall=70`, …), **not** the legacy 1..9 values. I reused `crate::error_private::{ERROR, ERR_isError, ZSTD_error_*}` accordingly; using the legacy values would have produced wrong error codes and a wrong `ERR_isError` threshold.\n\n### Translation notes\n- All bit/FSE/HUF machinery is local: `BIT_DStream_t`/`BIT_*`, `FSE_DTableHeader`/`FSE_decode_t`/`FSE_DState_t`/`FSE_buildDTable`/`FSE_readNCount`/`FSE_decompress*`, `HUF_DEltX2/X4`, `HUF_DDescX6`, `HUF_DSeqX6` (`#[repr(C)] union`), `HUF_readStats`, all X2/X4/X6 readers + stream decoders + `HUF_decompress` selector with the 16×3 `algoTime` table and the 3-entry fn-pointer array. Only `BYTE/U16/U32/S16/…`, `MEM_*` and libc externs come from `crate::cmem`.\n- `BIT_initDStream`'s `switch(srcSize)` fallthrough (cases 7→2) became a descending `if srcSize >= n` chain — exactly equivalent.\n- Compile-time-false static reload guards in `FSE_decompress_usingDTable_generic` (`FSE_MAX_TABLELOG*2+7 > 64`, `*4+7 > 64`) are dropped, as the C preprocessor/optimizer does.\n- The `HUF_DECODE_SYMBOLX{2,4,6}_{0,1,2}` macros are reproduced as `macro_rules!` preserving the `MEM_64bits()` runtime guards.\n- Shifts and arithmetic that can overflow use `wrapping_*` / `wrapping_shl` / `wrapping_shr` (x86 shift-masking semantics); pointer arithmetic that can go out of range uses `(p as usize).wrapping_add/sub(...)`.\n- `ZSTD_decompress` allocates the ~141 KB `ZSTD_DCtx` on the stack via `MaybeUninit` and sets only `base`, matching the C.\n- `assert`/`DISPLAY`/`DEBUGLOG` dropped; the commented-out `memset`s in `HUF_readDTableX2/X4/X6` and `HUF_readStats` left out as in C.\n\nThe remaining 76 crate-wide build errors are all in files owned by others (`compress/zstd_compress/p1-p3.rs`, `legacy/zstd_legacy.rs`, `legacy/v05.rs`, `dictbuilder/fastcover.rs`); none were touched. Because those are name-resolution failures that abort before type-checking, I additionally verified v02.rs in an isolated crate with only `cmem.rs` + `error_private.rs` — it compiles clean and links all 8 symbols.","usage":{"total_tokens":199166,"tool_uses":28,"duration_ms":1210724},"uuid":"2d89ffac-9cf3-4bab-b56e-f9357a45232b","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d"}
