r 21720 customMem 21728 litSize 21752 litBuffer 21760 headerBuffer 152840\n      ZBUFF 160 | lhSize 128 customMem 136 ; DDict 24 ; XXH64 88 ; FP 24 ; CM 24\nRust: identical on every field\n```\n\n### Key findings / decisions worth flagging\n\n1. **The brief's claim that this file embeds its own `static` XXH32/XXH64 is incorrect for v07.** `zstd_v07.c` only `#include`s `../common/xxhash.h` and calls `XXH64_reset/update/digest`, which `XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_` rewrites to the *external* `ZSTD_XXH64_*` symbols in `xxhash.c`. (That pattern holds for v05/v06, not v07 — verified with `grep -n XXH zstd_v07.c`: only the include plus 5 call sites.) So I used `crate::xxhash::{XXH64_state_t, ZSTD_XXH64_reset/update/digest}`, which is what the C actually links to, and defining a private copy would have been wrong.\n\n2. **Compile-time-false static tests were folded, as the C compiler does.** In `FSEv07_decompress_usingDTable_generic`, `FSEv07_MAX_TABLELOG*2+7 > 64` (31>64) and `*4+7 > 64` (55>64) are both false on x86-64, so the intermediate `BITv07_reloadDStream` calls — including the `{ if (reload > unfinished) { op+=2; break; } }` early exit — are absent. `MEM_64bits()`/`MEM_32bits()` guards are kept as runtime `if`s.\n\n3. **Two array indexes converted to raw pointers to avoid Rust panics where C had none:** `rankVal[consumed][w]` in `HUFv07_readDTableX4` (reachable index 16 on a 16-row table if a caller supplies `maxTableLog==16`) and `algoTime[Q]` in `HUFv07_selectDecoder`. Rust bounds checks are *not* disabled by `overflow-checks = false`, so these would have panicked instead of reproducing C's behaviour.\n\n4. **`goto`/fallthrough restructuring:** `ZSTDv07_decompressContinue`'s `getFrameHeaderSize -> decodeFrameHeader` fallthrough is handled by duplicating the 5-line header-decode body (no helper introduced, keeping the 1:1 function list). `ZBUFFv07_decompressContinue`'s three-way chained fallthrough (`loadHeader -> read -> load -> flush`) uses a `'dispatch: loop` with a `cur` stage variable: C `break` becomes `break 'dispatch`, C fallthrough becomes `cur = <next>; continue 'dispatch`, and the outer `while notDone` re-reads `zbd->stage` each iteration exactly as C's `switch` does.\n\n5. **Shift-width hazards:** `MEM_readLE32(ip) >> bitCount` in `FSEv07_readNCount` can have `bitCount >= 32` (the `bitCount += 16` path), which is UB in C and a hard error in Rust. I used `wrapping_shr`, which masks to `& 31` — exactly the x86 `shrl` behaviour gcc emits.\n\n6. **`ZSTDv07_copy4`/`copy8` are load-then-store of `u32`/`u64`** (`read_unaligned` + `write_unaligned`) rather than `copy_nonoverlapping`, because `ZSTDv07_wildcopy` legitimately copies overlapping match data and relies on the single-load/single-store shape gcc generates for `memcpy(d,s,8)`.\n\n7. `assert()` calls in `ZSTDv07_execSequence` were dropped per DEBUGLEVEL 0, as required.\n\nOnly `translation/src/legacy/v07.rs` was modified. The remaining crate errors at the time of writing belong to other files being worked on concurrently (`compress/zstdmt_compress.rs`, `legacy/zstd_legacy.rs`'s `v06` imports, `dictbuilder/*`); notably `zstd_legacy.rs`'s 16 previously-unresolved `v07` imports now all resolve, which confirms my module's public API is type-checked and matches its expected signatures."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":141,"cache_read_input_tokens":268372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":141,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019Eh7BwPKDFF1MGZY9fi8Yz","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d","uuid":"55d644b1-3e7d-4df2-b793-5b7dca60cde1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:38:57.788Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Port legacy zstd_v07.c"}
