enum; differential testing caught it immediately (C returned `-72`, Rust `-3`). Fixed, and the dead `ERR_strings`/`ERR_getErrorName` were dropped with an explanatory comment.\n\n### Differential validation against `libzstd.so` (both dlopen'd, results compared)\n| generator | inputs | byte-identical full decodes | mismatches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| random-after-magic + `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` | 400k | 803 | 0 |\n| shaped block/literal headers + streaming API | 400k | 47,127 (+200k streaming steps) | 0 |\n| forced HUF-RLE weight header | 400k | — | 0 |\n| forced FSE weight header / forced X4 selection | 558k | — | 0 |\n| HUF + *valid* all-RLE sequences section | 800k | 2,193 | 0 |\n\nReturn codes, output bytes, `nextSrcSizeToDecompress`/`decompressContinue`/`resetDCtx` results all matched everywhere.\n\n**Coverage** (gcov on the C original with the same generators): 69.8% + 79.9% across passes. Every function is entered, including the full double-symbol family (`HUF_readDTableX4`, `HUF_fillDTableX4`, `HUF_fillDTableX4Level2`, `HUF_decodeStreamX4`, `HUF_decodeLastSymbolX4`, `HUF_decompress4X4_usingDTable`) and `FSE_decompress_usingDTable_generic`.\n\n**Residual gap:** no frame using the X4 path ever *fully* decodes under synthetic input (all four bitstreams must terminate exactly, which needs a real v0.3 encoder). X4 is covered by error-code equivalence over ~1M inputs plus full line coverage, but not by byte-level output comparison. The X2 path is byte-verified.\n\n### Notable translation decisions\n- `BIT_initDStream`'s case-7-down-to-2 fallthrough → six cascading `if srcSize >= N` (exactly equivalent for the reachable range 1..7).\n- The two `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG*2+7 > sizeof(size_t)*8` / `*4+7` static tests are kept as const-folding `if`s; both are false on x86-64, so the extra reloads vanish as they do in C.\n- `HUF_DECODE_SYMBOLX2_0/1/2` and `X4_0/1/2` → `macro_rules!` so the `MEM_64bits()`/`HUF_MAX_TABLELOG<=12` guards and pointer post-increments stay literal.\n- `ZSTD_decompress` uses `MaybeUninit::<ZSTD_DCtx>::uninit()` and writes only `.base`, matching C's uninitialized ~132 KB stack context.\n- `BIT_highbit32` = `val.leading_zeros() ^ 31`, matching gcc's `__builtin_clz(val) ^ 31`; every call site has a non-zero argument guaranteed by a preceding check.\n- Shift amounts that C could push out of range (`1 << (tableLog-1)`, `1 << (sizeLog-nbBits)`) are masked `& 31` to reproduce x86 behaviour rather than risk a Rust shift-overflow panic.","usage":{"total_tokens":232374,"tool_uses":40,"duration_ms":1783259},"uuid":"647541c3-c414-4a75-ae6f-4e70e795a027","session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d"}
