{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2zdkohcauvrrlz6clg3y4k7cryrhph7zbr7catez7suq4wb3ee6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01KzaEjxofDoLbS45pr6TCCd","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Differential fuzz: entropy layer","prompt":"You are validating a Rust transliteration of zstd against the original C, in\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox.\n\nTwo shared libraries expose the SAME 615 symbols:\n  C:    c_src/build/libzstd.so\n  Rust: verify/rustlib/libzstd.so     (copy of translation/target/release/libzstd.so)\nAn example differential harness already exists: verify/harness.c, built as\n  gcc -w -O1 -o verify/harness_c  verify/harness.c -Ic_src/src/include -Lc_src/build     -l:libzstd.so -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/c_src/build\n  gcc -w -O1 -o verify/harness_rs verify/harness.c -Ic_src/src/include -Lverify/rustlib -l:libzstd.so -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/verify/rustlib\nand its two outputs are already byte-identical.\n\nYOUR TASK: write `verify/entropy.c`, a NEW differential harness that hammers the\n**low-level entropy / hashing / suffix-sort API** (which harness.c does not touch),\nbuild it twice exactly as above (producing verify/entropy_c and verify/entropy_rs),\nrun both, and `diff` the outputs. Report any mismatch with enough detail to fix it.\n\nThese functions are NOT in the public headers, so declare them yourself in the .c\n(they are all `extern \"C\"` in both libraries). Read the real prototypes from:\n  c_src/src/common/fse.h, c_src/src/common/huf.h, c_src/src/compress/hist.h,\n  c_src/src/common/xxhash.h (namespaced: ZSTD_XXH32/ZSTD_XXH64...),\n  c_src/src/dictBuilder/divsufsort.h, c_src/src/common/zstd_internal.h\nDo NOT #include those private headers directly if that drags in inline code —\nprefer hand-written `extern` declarations so that BOTH builds call through the .so.\n(You may #include them if it compiles and still resolves the calls to the .so;\nverify with `nm -u` that the symbols are undefined in the object.)\n\nCover at minimum, with deterministic pseudo-random inputs (xorshift64, fixed\nseeds) and a wide range of sizes/params — print for every call: the return value,\nplus an FNV-1a hash of every output buffer and of every by-reference output:\n\nFSE:  FSE_versionNumber, FSE_isError, FSE_getErrorName, FSE_compressBound,\n      FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, FSE_normalizeCount,\n      FSE_NCountWriteBound, FSE_writeNCount, FSE_readNCount, FSE_readNCount_bmi2,\n      FSE_buildCTable_wksp, FSE_buildCTable_rle, FSE_compress_usingCTable,\n      FSE_buildDTable_wksp, FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2\n      -> do full round trips (count -> normalize -> writeNCount -> readNCount ->\n         buildDTable -> decompress) AND feed *random/corrupt* buffers to\n         FSE_readNCount / FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2 / FSE_buildDTable_wksp so error\n         paths are compared too.\nHUF:  HUF_isError, HUF_getErrorName, HUF_compressBound, HUF_minTableLog,\n      HUF_cardinality, HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_buildCTable_wksp,\n      HUF_writeCTable_wksp, HUF_readCTable, HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable,\n      HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_validateCTable,\n      HUF_compress1X_usingCTable, HUF_compress4X_usingCTable,\n      HUF_compress1X_repeat, HUF_compress4X_repeat,\n      HUF_readStats, HUF_readStats_wksp, HUF_selectDecoder,\n      HUF_readDTableX1_wksp, HUF_readDTableX2_wksp,\n      HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable, HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable,\n      HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp,\n      HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly_wksp\n      -> full round trips at many tableLogs/maxSymbolValues and with all\n         combinations of the `flags` bitset values 0..63, PLUS corrupt-input runs.\n      (HUF_readCTableHeader returns a small struct by value — exercise it too and\n       print its fields.)\nHIST: HIST_isError, HIST_count, HIST_countFast, HIST_count_wksp,\n      HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_count_simple, HIST_add\nXXH:  ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber, ZSTD_XXH32, ZSTD_XXH64 and the full streaming APIs\n      (createState/reset/update in many chunk splittings/digest/copyState/\n       freeState/canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical) over many sizes 0..100000.\nSORT: divsufsort and divbwt — NOTE divbwt has 7 params:\n      `int divbwt(const unsigned char *T, unsigned char *U, int *A, int n,\n                  unsigned char *num_indexes, int *indexes, int openMP)`\n      (read c_src/src/dictBuilder/divsufsort.h to confirm). Compare the whole SA/U\n      arrays, pidx, num_indexes and indexes[] over many alphabets and sizes.\nMISC: ERR_getErrorString for codes 0..130, ZSTD_getErrorString,\n      ZSTD_versionNumber/String, ZSTD_isError, ZSTD_getErrorCode,\n      ZSTD_buildFSETable and ZSTD_decodeSeqHeaders if you can drive them safely\n      (they need a ZSTD_DCtx; skip if it requires private struct layout),\n      ZSTD_getcBlockSize, ZSTD_frameHeaderSize, ZSTD_isFrame, ZSTD_isSkippableFrame\n      on random buffers.\n\nRULES:\n- The harness must be fully deterministic (no time(), no addresses printed, no\n  uninitialised reads that could differ). Never print pointer values.\n- Allocate output buffers with malloc and memset them to a known pattern before\n  each call so that \"untouched bytes\" are comparable.\n- It is FINE (and desirable) for many calls to return errors — what matters is\n  that C and Rust return the SAME thing.\n- If a call reads uninitialised workspace by design (e.g. cwksp init-once\n  buffers), memset the workspace before each call so both sides agree.\n- Avoid inputs that make the C itself crash (that would just abort both). If you\n  find an input where C crashes, drop that input and note it.\n- Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes per binary.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n1. verify/entropy.c\n2. verify/entropy_c, verify/entropy_rs built and run; outputs\n   verify/out_entropy_c.txt and verify/out_entropy_rs.txt\n3. `diff` result. If the diff is non-empty, MINIMISE each distinct failure to a\n   tiny reproducer and report: the function, the exact arguments, the C result and\n   the Rust result. Do NOT attempt to fix the Rust translation yourself — just\n   report precisely.\nAlso report the number of distinct API calls compared."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":584030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2303,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d","uuid":"11c3a035-4ad4-451f-b918-d45863aaa20e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:55:40.233Z"}
