{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4wjlmbb7cmmlizmeo7ist3vcjat7skmdo7cei4kz5p3asylsetza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01XPXmh7Sz7mvHzqYJTjR7AT","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Differential fuzz: legacy decoders","prompt":"You are validating a Rust transliteration of zstd against the original C, in\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox.\n\nTwo shared libraries expose the SAME 615 symbols:\n  C:    c_src/build/libzstd.so\n  Rust: verify/rustlib/libzstd.so\nBuild pattern (see verify/harness.c for a working example):\n  gcc -w -O1 -o verify/legacy_c  verify/legacy.c -Ic_src/src/include -Lc_src/build     -l:libzstd.so -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/c_src/build\n  gcc -w -O1 -o verify/legacy_rs verify/legacy.c -Ic_src/src/include -Lverify/rustlib -l:libzstd.so -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/verify/rustlib\n\nYOUR TASK: write `verify/legacy.c`, a differential harness for the **legacy\ndecoders** (zstd v0.1 .. v0.7) and the deprecated ZBUFF APIs, build it twice,\nrun both, diff, and report mismatches precisely.\n\nDeclare the functions yourself with `extern`; the real prototypes are in\n  c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v01.h .. zstd_v07.h\n  c_src/src/deprecated/zbuff.h\nSymbols to cover (all exist in both .so files):\n  ZSTDv01_*: isError, decompress, decompressDCtx, findFrameSizeInfoLegacy,\n             createDCtx, freeDCtx, resetDCtx, nextSrcSizeToDecompress,\n             decompressContinue\n  ZSTDv02_*, ZSTDv03_*: isError, decompress, findFrameSizeInfoLegacy, createDCtx,\n             freeDCtx, resetDCtx, nextSrcSizeToDecompress, decompressContinue\n  ZSTDv04_*: decompress, decompressDCtx, findFrameSizeInfoLegacy, createDCtx,\n             freeDCtx, resetDCtx, nextSrcSizeToDecompress, decompressContinue\n  ZBUFFv04_*: createDCtx, freeDCtx, decompressInit, decompressWithDictionary,\n             decompressContinue, recommendedDInSize, recommendedDOutSize,\n             isError, getErrorName\n  ZSTDv05_*/v06_*/v07_*: the full exported set (copy the names from\n             /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/c_syms.txt,\n             e.g. `grep '^T ZSTDv05_' c_syms.txt`), plus FSEv05_*/FSEv06_*/FSEv07_*,\n             HUFv05_*/HUFv06_*/HUFv07_*, ZBUFFv05_*/v06_*/v07_*\n  and the modern entry points that dispatch into legacy:\n             ZSTD_decompress / ZSTD_getFrameContentSize / ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize\n             / ZSTD_decompressStream on buffers carrying legacy magic numbers.\n\nLegacy magic numbers (little-endian first 4 bytes of a frame):\n  v0.1 uses a 3-byte magic 0xFD2FB5 with the 4th byte being the version nibble;\n  read `ZSTDv01_isError`/`ZSTDv01_decompress` and c_src/src/legacy/zstd_legacy.h\n  (`ZSTD_isLegacy`) to get the exact detection rules — reproduce them in the\n  harness so you generate buffers that are actually *recognised* as each version.\n  v0.5=0xFD2FB525, v0.6=0xFD2FB526, v0.7=0xFD2FB527 (verify in the sources).\n\nSTRATEGY (we have no real legacy-format encoder, so use structured fuzzing):\n1. For each version, build ~200k deterministic pseudo-random buffers (xorshift64,\n   fixed seed) of sizes 0..4096 that start with that version's magic, plus some\n   with deliberately valid-looking frame/block/literals headers so that deeper\n   code paths (FSE/HUF table reading, sequence decoding) are reached.\n2. Call each entry point on each buffer and print: return value (or error name),\n   and an FNV-1a hash of the output buffer plus the number of bytes written.\n3. Also drive the *streaming* legacy paths: ZBUFFv0x_decompressInit +\n   repeated ZBUFFv0x_decompressContinue with small in/out chunks, and\n   ZSTDv0x_createDCtx + nextSrcSizeToDecompress/decompressContinue loops.\n   Print every intermediate return value and hint size.\n4. Exercise the dictionary variants (ZSTDv05/06/07_decompress_usingDict,\n   ZBUFFv0x_decompressInitDictionary, ZSTDv07_createDDict/freeDDict/\n   decompress_usingDDict, ZSTDv07_getDecompressedSize, ZSTDv0x_getFrameParams,\n   ZSTDv0x_sizeofDCtx, ZSTDv0x_copyDCtx, ZSTDv0x_decompressBlock,\n   ZSTDv0x_insertBlock, ZSTDv07_isSkipFrame, ZSTDv07_estimateDCtxSize).\n5. Exercise FSEv0x_/HUFv0x_ directly: createDTable/freeDTable/readNCount/\n   buildDTable/buildDTable_raw/buildDTable_rle/decompress/decompress_usingDTable,\n   HUFv0x_readDTableX2/X4 + all the decompressNXM variants, HUFv07_readStats,\n   HUFv07_selectDecoder — on both well-formed and random inputs.\n\nRULES:\n- Fully deterministic; never print pointers or uninitialised memory.\n- memset output buffers to a known pattern before every call.\n- Errors are expected and fine — what matters is C == Rust.\n- If some input makes the *C* library crash, exclude it and note it in the report\n  (do not spend long on it). Use a small wrapper that limits sizes to keep the\n  C side from obvious OOB: prefer generously-sized output buffers.\n- Runtime under ~6 minutes per binary. Split the work into phases and print a\n  phase banner so a diff localises quickly.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n1. verify/legacy.c\n2. verify/legacy_c and verify/legacy_rs built, run; outputs\n   verify/out_legacy_c.txt / verify/out_legacy_rs.txt\n3. The diff. For every distinct mismatch, minimise to a tiny reproducer and report\n   the function, exact input bytes (hex), the C result and the Rust result.\n   Do NOT modify anything under translation/ — only report.\nReport how many calls were compared and the mismatch count."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6612,"cache_read_input_tokens":586333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6612,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d","uuid":"12c5c300-c11b-433c-aa53-ed8ee06d279d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:56:10.887Z"}
