ress,\n   ZSTD_decompressContinue, ZSTD_nextInputType, ZSTD_copyDCtx, ZSTD_insertBlock,\n   ZSTD_decompressBlock, ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min.\n7. Sequence APIs: ZSTD_generateSequences, ZSTD_sequenceBound,\n   ZSTD_mergeBlockDelimiters, ZSTD_compressSequences with BOTH\n   ZSTD_sf_noBlockDelimiters and ZSTD_sf_explicitBlockDelimiters,\n   ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals, ZSTD_convertBlockSequences,\n   ZSTD_get1BlockSummary, ZSTD_getSeqStore, ZSTD_seqToCodes,\n   ZSTD_registerSequenceProducer(cctx, NULL, NULL).\n8. Multi-frame / skippable / checksum: concatenated frames, ZSTD_findDecompressedSize,\n   ZSTD_decompressBound, ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize, ZSTD_writeSkippableFrame /\n   ZSTD_readSkippableFrame for all 16 magic variants, checksum mismatch handling,\n   ZSTD_d_forceIgnoreChecksum, ZSTD_d_maxBlockSize, ZSTD_d_windowLogMax,\n   ZSTD_d_disableHuffmanAssembly, ZSTD_decompressionMargin.\n9. Deprecated wrappers: ZSTD_initCStream{,_srcSize,_usingDict,_advanced,\n   _usingCDict,_usingCDict_advanced}, ZSTD_resetCStream, ZSTD_initDStream{,_usingDict,\n   _usingDDict}, ZSTD_resetDStream, ZSTD_compress_advanced,\n   ZSTD_compress_advanced_internal, ZSTD_compress_usingCDict_advanced,\n   ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_deprecated, ZSTD_compressContinue_public,\n   ZSTD_compressEnd_public, ZSTD_compressBlock_deprecated,\n   ZSTD_decompressBlock_deprecated, ZSTD_toFlushNow, ZSTD_getFrameProgression.\n10. The whole deprecated ZBUFF API (c_src/src/deprecated/zbuff.h): ZBUFF_createCCtx\n    {,_advanced}, ZBUFF_compressInit{,Dictionary,_advanced}, ZBUFF_compressContinue,\n    ZBUFF_compressFlush, ZBUFF_compressEnd, ZBUFF_recommendedC{In,Out}Size,\n    ZBUFF_createDCtx{,_advanced}, ZBUFF_decompressInit{,Dictionary},\n    ZBUFF_decompressContinue, ZBUFF_recommendedD{In,Out}Size, ZBUFF_isError,\n    ZBUFF_getErrorName — full round trips with several chunk sizes.\n11. ZSTDMT (multithreading is compiled OUT, so behaviour should be trivial):\n    ZSTDMT_createCCtx_advanced(1, cmem, NULL) must return NULL in both; and\n    ZSTDMT_freeCCtx(NULL) must return 0 in both. Do NOT call the other ZSTDMT_*\n    entry points with a NULL context (that would deref NULL in both libraries).\n12. COVER internals: COVER_sum, COVER_computeEpochs, COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus,\n    COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize, COVER_best_init/start/finish/wait/destroy,\n    COVER_dictSelectionError/IsError/Free, COVER_selectDict — declare them from\n    c_src/src/dictBuilder/cover.h and drive them directly.\n13. ZDICT: ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer, ZDICT_finalizeDictionary with several\n    ZDICT_params_t, ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize, ZDICT_getDictID, ZDICT_isError,\n    ZDICT_getErrorName, and all four trainers with several parameter sets\n    (including nbThreads=1..4 which is a no-op here, and splitPoint variants).\n14. ZSTD_CCtx_trace(cctx, 0) and ZSTD_CCtx_reset with all three ZSTD_ResetDirective\n    values; ZSTD_CCtx_refThreadPool(cctx, NULL); ZSTD_CCtx_setCParams /\n    setFParams / setParams; ZSTD_adjustCParams / ZSTD_checkCParams / ZSTD_cycleLog\n    over a big grid; ZSTD_getCParams / ZSTD_getParams over a big grid.\n\nRULES:\n- Fully deterministic (xorshift64 PRNG with fixed seeds). NEVER print pointer\n  values, addresses, or uninitialised memory. Print FNV-1a hashes of buffers.\n- memset output buffers to a known pattern before each call.\n- Errors are expected and fine — only C vs Rust equality matters.\n- Skip any input that crashes the C library, and note it.\n- Keep runtime under ~6 minutes per binary. Print phase banners.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n1. verify/adv.c\n2. verify/adv_c and verify/adv_rs built and run; outputs verify/out_adv_c.txt and\n   verify/out_adv_rs.txt\n3. The diff. For every distinct mismatch, minimise to a small reproducer and report\n   the function, exact arguments, C result and Rust result.\n   Do NOT modify anything under translation/ — only report.\nReport how many calls were compared and the mismatch count."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequen