{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hwnmmwgbp7nzoeuosuysbbn66xn52b72rebtgjjysdwndiqo54zq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01PjhR2pdxzLBfvVpSJYLcqU","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Restore dictBuilder stderr output","prompt":"You are polishing a Rust transliteration of zstd in\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/translation.\n\nCONTEXT\nThe crate is a faithful transliteration of c_src/. It builds\n(`cd translation && cargo build --release`) and exports exactly the same 615\nsymbols as the C build, with byte-identical behaviour on three differential\nharnesses. Read\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/PORTING_GUIDE.md first.\n\nONE KNOWN GAP: the three dictBuilder translations dropped the `DISPLAY` /\n`DISPLAYLEVEL` / `DISPLAYUPDATE` / `LOCALDISPLAYLEVEL` / `LOCALDISPLAYUPDATE`\nstderr writes. The C library therefore imports `fprintf`, `fputc`, `fwrite`,\n`fflush`, `stderr` and `clock` (see `nm -D -u c_src/build/libzstd.so`) while the\nRust one does not, and any caller that passes a non-zero `notificationLevel`\n(e.g. `ZDICT_params_t.notificationLevel`, `ZDICT_cover_params_t.zParams\n.notificationLevel`, `ZDICT_fastCover_params_t.zParams.notificationLevel`) gets\ndiagnostics from C but nothing from Rust.\n\nYOUR TASK: restore those writes so the stderr output is byte-identical to the C.\n\nFILES YOU MAY EDIT (only these):\n  translation/src/dictbuilder/zdict.rs\n  translation/src/dictbuilder/cover.rs\n  translation/src/dictbuilder/fastcover.rs\n  translation/src/cmem.rs        (only to add the libc externs listed below)\n\nHOW\n1. Add to `translation/src/cmem.rs` (or a small new private helper in each\n   dictbuilder file — your choice, but prefer cmem.rs so it is shared):\n   ```rust\n   unsafe extern \"C\" {\n       pub static mut stderr: *mut c_void;               // FILE*\n       pub fn fprintf(stream: *mut c_void, fmt: *const c_char, ...) -> c_int;\n       pub fn fflush(stream: *mut c_void) -> c_int;\n       pub fn clock() -> core::ffi::c_long;\n   }\n   ```\n   (`stderr` on glibc is a real `FILE*` object symbol, so `static mut stderr:\n   *mut c_void` is correct — verify by linking and running.)\n   Because we call the SAME `fprintf` with the SAME format string and the SAME\n   arguments, the bytes produced are identical by construction. Do NOT reimplement\n   printf formatting in Rust.\n2. In each dictbuilder file, define macros mirroring the C ones exactly. Study the\n   C definitions first:\n   - c_src/src/dictBuilder/zdict.c lines ~70-90\n   - c_src/src/dictBuilder/cover.c (its DISPLAY/DISPLAYLEVEL/LOCALDISPLAYLEVEL/\n     DISPLAYUPDATE/LOCALDISPLAYUPDATE and the `g_time`/`g_refreshRate`/\n     `g_displayLevel` statics and `COVER_setDisplayLevel`-style plumbing)\n   - c_src/src/dictBuilder/fastcover.c (same set)\n   Note carefully WHICH level variable each macro tests (`notificationLevel`,\n   `g_displayLevel`, or a local `displayLevel`) — they differ between files and\n   between the `LOCAL*` and non-`LOCAL*` variants.\n   A Rust equivalent:\n   ```rust\n   macro_rules! DISPLAY {\n       ($($arg:tt)*) => { unsafe {\n           crate::cmem::fprintf(crate::cmem::stderr, $($arg)*);\n           crate::cmem::fflush(crate::cmem::stderr);\n       } };\n   }\n   ```\n   used as `DISPLAY!(c\"...\\n\".as_ptr(), args...)` — or build the NUL-terminated\n   format string with `concat!(..., \"\\0\").as_ptr() as *const c_char`.\n3. Restore EVERY dropped call site, with the same format string (byte for byte,\n   including `%u`, `%zu`, `%f`, `%.2f`, `%4u`, `%s`, `%c`, `\\r`, `\\n`, `%%`...) and\n   the same arguments in the same order and the same C types:\n   - `unsigned` -> pass `c_uint`\n   - `size_t`   -> pass `usize`\n   - `double`   -> pass `f64`\n   - `int`      -> pass `c_int`\n   - `char*`    -> pass `*const c_char`\n   Cast at each call site exactly as the C does. Grep the C for `DISPLAY` in each\n   file and work through the list; there are roughly 41 in zdict.c, 36 in cover.c\n   and 35 in fastcover.c.\n4. Restore the `clock()`-based throttling that `DISPLAYUPDATE` /\n   `LOCALDISPLAYUPDATE` use (`g_time`, `g_refreshRate`, `ZDICT_clockSpan`,\n   `COVER_clockSpan`-style helpers) so the *number* of update lines matches.\n   `clock_t` is `long` on Linux; `CLOCKS_PER_SEC` is 1000000.\n   NOTE: `clock()` output is wall/CPU-time dependent, so lines emitted by\n   `DISPLAYUPDATE` are inherently non-deterministic in BOTH libraries. Restore\n   them faithfully anyway (same code shape), but do not try to make them match\n   run-to-run.\n5. Also double-check `g_displayLevel` handling: in cover.c and fastcover.c it is a\n   file-scope `static int g_displayLevel` that gets assigned from\n   `parameters.zParams.notificationLevel`, and is *read* by\n   `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus` and copied into worker params. Make sure the Rust\n   preserves that data flow (some of it may already be there).\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n- Do NOT change any algorithmic behaviour, return value, or buffer content.\n- Do NOT touch any file outside the four listed above.\n- Keep `cargo build --release` clean (no errors; warnings acceptable).\n\nVERIFY\n1. `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/translation && cargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -20` — must succeed.\n2. `cp translation/target/release/libzstd.so verify/rustlib/`\n3. Confirm the symbol set is still exactly equal:\n   `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox/verify/diff_syms.sh`\n   must report 615/615 and no missing/extra.\n4. Confirm the three existing harnesses are still byte-identical:\n   ```\n   cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oyxCox\n   ./verify/harness_rs > verify/out_rs.txt && diff verify/out_c.txt verify/out_rs.txt && echo HARNESS-OK\n   ./verify/big_rs     > verify/out_big_rs.txt && diff verify/out_big_c.txt verify/out_big_rs.txt && echo BIG-OK\n   ```\n5. Write a small C program `verify/disp.c` that calls\n   `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy`, `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover`,\n   `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover`, `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover`,\n   `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover` and `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary`\n   with `notificationLevel = 4` on a small deterministic corpus, build it against\n   both .so files (same pattern as verify/harness.c), run both capturing **stderr\n   only** (`2> file 1>/dev/null`), and diff. Filter out lines containing `\\r`\n   progress updates / elapsed-time numbers if they are timing dependent, and\n   report how much of the stderr now matches.\n\nREPORT: number of DISPLAY sites restored per file, the build/symbol/harness\nverification results, and the stderr diff outcome (including which lines remain\ntiming dependent)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":606503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1672,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9325aeb1-fde7-405e-a2e0-217179ef0d1d","uuid":"8832a4b8-07de-4533-b389-87b536761d4b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:59:14.390Z"}
