\nCompile-time `const _: () = assert!(...)` checks pin `sizeof`/`offsetof` of `ZSTD_CCtx` (5280), `ZSTD_DCtx` (95992), `ZSTD_CDict`, `ZSTD_DDict` and 30 more against the C, since they leak through `ZSTD_estimate*Size`/`ZSTD_sizeof_*`.\n\n## Two real bugs found and fixed by the harnesses\n1. **`FSEv04/05_readNCount`** — `if count >= threshold as i16` truncated `threshold` (32768 → −32768), flipping the comparison. C promotes the `short` to `int`. Fixed in `legacy/v04.rs`, `legacy/v05.rs`.\n2. **`FSE_minTableLog`** — `BIT_highbit32(0)` is UB (`__builtin_clz(0)`); GCC emits a bare `bsr`, which leaves its destination untouched, so the reference build reads a *different* leftover register in each of the two inlined copies. Reproduced per call site from the reference disassembly (documented in `fse_compress.rs`), fixing `FSE_optimalTableLog{,_internal}` and `FSE_normalizeCount` for `maxSymbolValue == 0`.\n\n## Notes\n- Build config honoured throughout: `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`, `DYNAMIC_BMI2=0` (no BMI2/asm variants), no `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` (pool/threading are no-ops, `ZSTDMT_createCCtx_advanced` returns NULL), `DEBUGLEVEL=0` (asserts/DEBUGLOG dropped), `ZSTD_ARCH_X86_SSE2` on (row match-finder uses SSE2 intrinsics) / `ZSTD_ARCH_X86_AVX2` off, `ZSTD_TRACE=1` with permanently-NULL hooks.\n- Known C bugs preserved verbatim, e.g. `zstd_opt.c:1391`'s `} {` instead of `} else {`, `ZSTD_ldm_gear_reset`'s missing write-back, `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`'s one-byte overwrite. Inputs that trap in C (divide-by-zero in `ZSTD_ldm_getMaxNbSeq`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable` OOB) trap in Rust at the same call with identical preceding output.\n- `c_src/` is untouched; the reference C build lives in `verify/cbuild/`. Re-run everything with `./verify/run_all.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":720000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"